for r in eos:lines.append(f"| {r['seed']} | {r['threshold']} | {r['main_caps']} | {r['calibrated_caps']} | {r['main_j2j']*100:.3f} | {r['calibrated_j2j']*100:.3f} |")
lines+=['',f"Across adapter seeds, teacher matched-joint L2={np.mean([r['teacher_matched_l2'] for r in coords]):.4f}; GT-rig-supported candidate control={np.mean([r['gt_rig_supported_teacher_l2'] for r in coords]):.4f}. Restricting candidates to GT-rig support is an oracle diagnostic and did not repair the sequence localization. GT quantized-joint to rig-voxel-center distance={np.mean([r['gt_joint_to_rig_voxel_distance'] for r in coords]):.4f}, versus free joints={np.mean([r['free_joint_to_rig_voxel_distance'] for r in coords]):.4f}. EOS/quantization alone do not explain the remaining coordinate error.",'','## What remains unmatched','', '- Native kernels retain original weights/architecture, but no original CUDA rendering parity run exists. Actual features are DINO-L/reg x_prenorm; four native224 neutral views are upsampled518 and point-pooled, unlike full original rendering/preprocessing.','- Adapter stage freezes mesh backbone; subsequent short stage updates full rig+mesh weights but uses only250 steps and16-cube geometry patches every8 steps after a2000-step warm start. Not original convergence or full rendering/normal/color loss.','- Occupancy VAEs are frozen official transfer models; no original24-hour retraining. The four generator networks are compact newly trained conv/attention models, not pretrained TRELLIS flow transformers.','- AR/skin heads remain small width64/two layers; exact coordinate-head factorization and EOS weighting are implementation assumptions. Full-vertex skin inference uses512-query chunks.','- Source cohort is25/6/10 with availability/registration exclusions, not the full benchmark. No labels, textures, retargeting, official baselines or complete original figure/table match.','', '[Rebuild, source hashes, numerical checks and strict inference boundaries](../../docs/round3_experiments.md). All unfavorable seeds and earlier exploratory paths remain available.']
